description:
ShapeDisplayObject has an alpha field (packages/core/src/engine/types.ts line 336), and it is used in tween interpolation (timeline-query.ts line 304 sets alpha: result.alpha / 100).

However, in packages/swf/src/compile.ts the alpha value is silently dropped for shapes:

1. colorEffectKey() (line 905): early return null for type !== instance/text/bitmap — shape alpha is not tracked
2. isFirst path (lines 1758-1772): only handles visible===false (zero-alpha CXForm) and blendMode/cacheAsBitmap/filters — no path to emit CXForm for standalone alpha

This means a shape tweened from alpha=1 to alpha=0 will render at full opacity throughout in Ruffle.

Fix needed in compile.ts:
1. In colorEffectKey(): add alpha tracking for type === 'shape' (like instance/bitmap at lines 911-921)
2. In the shape isFirst path (after the visible===false branch, before the final else): add:
   if (displayObj.alpha !== undefined && displayObj.alpha !== 1) {
     const alphaCXForm = { redMult:256, greenMult:256, blueMult:256, alphaMult: Math.round(Math.max(0,Math.min(1,displayObj.alpha))*256), redAdd:0,greenAdd:0,blueAdd:0,alphaAdd:0 };
     emit encodePlaceObject2WithCXForm(charId, depth, x, y, alphaCXForm, objTransform);
   }
3. Same fix needed in the posChanged update path for shapes (around line 2227)
